      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Given the screenshot attached you appear to have had broken network IDs. Hence opening the utility fixing them.\n\nWhen a build&test bundle fails to be created, it will load the previously cached one, regardless of the scene. This behaviour has been around forever and isn't really considered a bug - it's sort of how Unity does bundle building.\n\nI'll forward this to our SDK team to potentially not load any bundles when building fails, but I wouldn't expect this to be a priority task given it's been around forever.\n\nAs for why your original build failed, that's very hard to say without logs from that build where it failed and looking at your scene setup.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
