  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I opened an entirely different demo scene to look at how something was set up, and ran the offline testing with that scene.  When I was finished I opened up my original scene and tried to run an offline test, and it keeps opening the previous scene I was just looking at before.  The information in the SDK Control panel is showing everything correct, it just keeps opening the previous scene no matter what I try to do.  Unity 2022.3.22f1 and SDK 3.6.0.  I tried restarting unity, I tried manually selecting the world in the content manager tab (it was correctly selected) I tried reloading the SDK, I tried detaching the pipeline ID and pasting it back, and finally I completely deleted the scene it keeps opening with offline testing, the world component, and closed and restarted unity and nothing has changed it keeps loading the scene I was looking at before which is not even open anywhere and has been deleted.  I even rolled back to SDK 3.5.2 and it's still opening a completely different scene than I have open that doesn't even exist anymore in this project I am so lost.  I am afraid to even upload this world now in fear it will upload this other scene.",
